{
  "info": {
    "name": "CRM \u2014 Website Lead Capture",
    "description": "Website inquiry capture for ieagents.co.in.\n\nONE endpoint: POST /api/method/xbr_crm.api.web_lead.capture_inquiry\n\nSetup\n-----\n1. Open the collection Variables tab.\n2. Set `base_url` (default http://localhost:8001).\n3. Set `api_key` to the secret from the CRM Web Lead Key record.\n\nThe key is sent as the `X-Lead-Api-Key` header on every request, inherited from collection-level auth-free headers set per request.\n\nNotes\n-----\n- Frappe wraps every response in {\"message\": {...}} \u2014 read response.message, not the top level.\n- `duplicate: true` is a SUCCESS, not an error: the person already enquired and the new answers were attached to their existing lead as a note.\n- Requests 1 and 5 share {{dup_email}}/{{dup_mobile}} so you can prove dedup: run 'Consultation' then 'Duplicate \u2014 same email'.\n- Rate limit is 30 requests/minute per IP. Running the whole folder repeatedly will eventually return 429, which is correct behaviour.\n\nZapier\n------\nRequests 12 and 13 cover the Zapier path: retries are idempotent for 10 minutes (same key + form_type + email/mobile), and every error body carries a stable `code` to branch on.\n\nEnvironments\n------------\nDev : http://localhost:8001\nLive: https://crm.psdigitise.com\nSwitch with the `base_url` collection variable. The key differs per environment \u2014 a key created on the dev bench does not exist on live.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8001",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "CRM base URL, no trailing slash. Dev: http://localhost:8001 \u2014 Live: https://crm.psdigitise.com"
    },
    {
      "key": "api_key",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Value for X-Lead-Api-Key. Get it from the CRM Web Lead Key record."
    },
    {
      "key": "endpoint",
      "value": "/api/method/xbr_crm.api.web_lead.capture_inquiry",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "dup_email",
      "value": "postman.dedup@example.com",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Shared by the dedup pair. Change it to re-run dedup from a clean slate."
    },
    {
      "key": "dup_mobile",
      "value": "9876500123",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Fresh identity per request, so repeated runs do not all collide on",
          "// the dedup rule and report false 'duplicate' results.",
          "const n = Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8);",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set('rand', n);",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set('rand_email', `postman.${n}@example.com`);",
          "// Valid Indian mobile: 10 digits starting 6-9.",
          "const mobile = '9' + Math.floor(100000000 + Math.random() * 899999999);",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set('rand_mobile', mobile);"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Applies to every request in the collection.",
          "pm.test('response is JSON', () => pm.response.json());",
          "if (pm.response.code === 401) {",
          "    console.log('401 \u2014 check the api_key collection variable');",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Consultation form \u2014 creates a lead",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "X-Lead-Api-Key",
            "value": "{{api_key}}"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"form_type\": \"consultation\",\n  \"first_name\": \"arun\",\n  \"last_name\": \"kumar\",\n  \"email\": \"{{dup_email}}\",\n  \"mobile_no\": \"98765 00123\",\n  \"city\": \"Chennai\",\n  \"page_url\": \"https://ieagents.co.in/\",\n  \"utm_source\": \"google\",\n  \"utm_medium\": \"cpc\",\n  \"utm_campaign\": \"study-abroad-2026\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}{{endpoint}}",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}{{endpoint}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "The 'Book Free Consultation' popup. Note the deliberately messy input: lowercase names and a spaced mobile. The response lead will have 'Arun Kumar' and '+919876500123'."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const b = pm.response.json().message;",
              "pm.test('success', () => pm.expect(b.success).to.be.true);",
              "pm.test('a lead name came back', () => pm.expect(b.lead).to.be.a('string'));",
              "if (!b.duplicate) {",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('first_lead', b.lead);",
              "    console.log('created', b.lead);",
              "} else {",
              "    console.log('already existed ->', b.lead, '(change dup_email to start clean)');",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('first_lead', b.lead);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
