    {
      "name": "12. Zapier retry \u2014 identical resend, no new lead",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "X-Lead-Api-Key",
            "value": "{{api_key}}"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"form_type\": \"consultation\",\n  \"first_name\": \"Arun\",\n  \"email\": \"{{dup_email}}\",\n  \"mobile_no\": \"98765 00123\",\n  \"city\": \"\",\n  \"last_name\": \"null\",\n  \"zap_id\": \"01HXYZ-example\",\n  \"Raw Body\": \"{...}\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}{{endpoint}}",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}{{endpoint}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "RUN REQUEST 1 FIRST, then send this one TWICE.\n\nShaped the way Zapier actually posts:\n- `city` is an empty string (unmapped field)\n- `last_name` is the literal word \"null\"\n- `zap_id` and `Raw Body` are fields we do not know about\n\nAll three are tolerated: blanks and blank-words are treated as missing, unknown fields are ignored.\n\nThe retry behaviour: an identical submission (same key + form_type + email/mobile) within 10 minutes returns the ORIGINAL lead with duplicate:true and writes no second note. Send it 3 times \u2014 the lead name never changes and the lead's note count stays put."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const b = pm.response.json().message;",
              "pm.test('success', () => pm.expect(b.success).to.be.true);",
              "pm.test('duplicate:true', () => pm.expect(b.duplicate).to.be.true);",
              "const first = pm.collectionVariables.get('first_lead');",
              "if (first) pm.test('same lead as request 1', () => pm.expect(b.lead).to.eql(first));",
              "console.log('lead:', b.lead, '\u2014 send again, it must not change');"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
